# Shell scripts and the Makefile must stay LF in the repository. Git's
# autocrlf would otherwise hand a CRLF shebang to a Linux host, and
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with "bad interpreter" — a confusing failure
# for something that looks like a line-ending detail.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf

# Go source is LF everywhere.
*.go        text eol=lf
*.mod       text eol=lf
*.sum       text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one thing that is happier with CRLF on Windows.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Markdown and web assets: normalise on commit, leave the checkout alone.
*.md        text
*.js        text
*.css       text
*.html      text

# Binaries are never touched.
*.tar.gz    binary
*.exe       binary
